WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.370 --> 01:34.940
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.250 --> 01:37.800
[Episode 17]

4
01:49.660 --> 01:50.830
[Mao Zedong, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

5
01:50.860 --> 01:51.979
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

6
02:37.670 --> 02:39.700
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

7
03:07.560 --> 03:08.430
Here.

8
03:09.470 --> 03:10.530
Comrade Jiaxiang,

9
03:10.640 --> 03:13.240
this recliner was specially prepared for you.

10
03:13.560 --> 03:15.020
Thank you, Comrade Enlai.

11
03:17.040 --> 03:17.630
Comrade Kai Feng.

12
03:17.630 --> 03:18.290
Have a seat.

13
03:19.079 --> 03:20.079
Come here.

14
03:20.400 --> 03:20.710
Comrades,

15
03:20.710 --> 03:22.280
sit anywhere you like.

16
03:22.480 --> 03:23.320
Come on.

17
03:23.640 --> 03:24.900
Commander-in-Chief.

18
03:25.350 --> 03:26.610
Commander-in-Chief.

19
03:27.020 --> 03:28.480
Comrade Shaoqi, sit down.

20
03:30.800 --> 03:32.930
Commander-in-Chief, please come in.

21
03:36.520 --> 03:37.810
Here, Commander Peng.

22
03:37.840 --> 03:39.400
Comrade Zedong, sit here.

23
03:40.020 --> 03:41.390
Come here.

24
03:41.840 --> 03:42.400
Luofu.

25
03:42.530 --> 03:44.060
Comrade Zedong, come here.

26
03:55.630 --> 03:56.750
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

27
03:56.810 --> 03:58.190
[Zhu De, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

28
03:58.190 --> 03:59.930
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

29
03:58.390 --> 04:00.020
Comrades, sit down quickly.

30
04:39.680 --> 04:41.290
Comrade Enlai, shall we begin?

31
04:41.290 --> 04:42.260
Alright.

32
04:44.800 --> 04:45.950
Comrades,

33
04:47.159 --> 04:48.560
let's start the meeting.

34
04:49.510 --> 04:51.000
Out of all 11 members

35
04:51.240 --> 04:53.040
of the Political Bureau,

36
04:53.630 --> 04:55.630
Comrades Wang Ming and Kang Sheng

37
04:56.240 --> 04:58.070
are stationed at the Comintern in Moscow.

38
04:58.070 --> 05:00.870
Comrade Zhang Guotao is in the Sichuan-Shaanxi Soviet Area.

39
05:00.870 --> 05:03.190
Comrade Ren Bishi is in Hunan-Hubei-Sichuan-Guizhou.

40
05:03.190 --> 05:06.680
Comrade Xiang Ying stayed behind in the Central Soviet Area.

41
05:07.160 --> 05:09.770
[Deng Xiaoping, Secretary General of the CPC Central Committee]

42
05:07.430 --> 05:09.230
We have 6 members present today.

43
05:09.430 --> 05:11.630
In addition, out of 5 alternate members

44
05:11.630 --> 05:13.310
of the Political Bureau,

45
05:13.800 --> 05:15.510
4 are present today.

46
05:16.120 --> 05:19.980
Representatives from the Red Army Corps and the central authorities

47
05:20.210 --> 05:21.300
are also here.

48
05:21.710 --> 05:23.680
Comrade Li De is attending as a non-voting delegate.

49
05:23.680 --> 05:25.920
This enlarged meeting of the Political Bureau

50
05:25.920 --> 05:27.160
has 2 main items on the agenda.

51
05:27.080 --> 05:30.070
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

52
05:27.480 --> 05:28.680
The first item is

53
05:29.040 --> 05:31.310
to revise the resolution made at the Liping Meeting

54
05:31.310 --> 05:32.840
on establishing a base area

55
05:32.870 --> 05:34.870
centered around northern Guizhou,

56
05:35.270 --> 05:37.870
and instead establish one in northwestern Sichuan.

57
05:37.870 --> 05:39.800
This agenda item is mainly based on

58
05:39.870 --> 05:42.470
the proposal by Comrade Liu Bocheng and Comrade Nie Rongzhen.

59
05:42.470 --> 05:44.590
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

60
05:42.580 --> 05:43.680
We bring their proposal

61
05:43.680 --> 05:44.800
to the meeting

62
05:44.950 --> 05:47.460
for everyone to discuss and vote on.

63
05:45.620 --> 05:47.340
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

64
05:48.120 --> 05:51.000
The second item on today's agenda is

65
05:52.000 --> 05:53.750
to summarize the lessons learned in military command

66
05:53.750 --> 05:56.310
since the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign

67
05:56.310 --> 05:59.510
and the strategic transfer.

68
06:00.680 --> 06:01.540
Comrade Luofu,

69
06:01.830 --> 06:02.690
Comrade Enlai,

70
06:02.990 --> 06:04.990
do you have any different opinions

71
06:05.240 --> 06:06.770
on today's agenda setting?

72
06:06.950 --> 06:07.810
No objections.

73
06:07.870 --> 06:09.420
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

74
06:08.030 --> 06:09.760
No objections. Let's proceed.

75
06:09.800 --> 06:10.600
Alright then.

76
06:10.750 --> 06:13.120
Let's begin with the first item on the agenda.

77
06:13.120 --> 06:15.000
We invite Comrade Liu Bocheng as the representative

78
06:15.000 --> 06:15.630
to explain

79
06:15.650 --> 06:17.980
the opinions of you and Comrade Rongzhen.

80
06:18.570 --> 06:19.570
Alright.

81
06:19.600 --> 06:20.400
My proposal is

82
06:20.410 --> 06:22.900
based on the specific situation in northern Guizhou.

83
06:22.900 --> 06:25.080
Although the reactionary forces here are relatively weak,

84
06:25.080 --> 06:26.220
it is sparsely populated

85
06:26.220 --> 06:27.240
and economically backward.

86
06:27.240 --> 06:29.640
It's also inhabited by ethnic minorities,

87
06:29.800 --> 06:32.110
and the foundation of our Party's work is quite poor,

88
06:32.110 --> 06:33.870
which is not conducive to our work.

89
06:33.870 --> 06:35.190
Considering all the above,

90
06:35.190 --> 06:37.190
Comrade Rongzhen and I both believe

91
06:37.240 --> 06:40.510
that the conditions in northern Guizhou are poor in all aspects,

92
06:40.510 --> 06:42.190
making it unfavorable for establishing a base area.

93
06:42.190 --> 06:44.940
However, if our Central Red Army crosses the Yangtze River to the north

94
06:44.940 --> 06:47.900
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

95
06:45.120 --> 06:46.920
and establishes a base area in northwestern Sichuan,

96
06:46.920 --> 06:48.360
there will be numerous advantages.

97
06:48.360 --> 06:50.070
First, it is densely populated

98
06:50.070 --> 06:51.310
and rich in resources,

99
06:51.310 --> 06:54.070
which facilitates the supply and development of our troops.

100
06:54.070 --> 06:56.270
Second, we can join forces with the 4th Front Army,

101
06:56.270 --> 06:58.270
and echo the Sichuan-Shaanxi base.

102
06:58.480 --> 06:59.159
Third,

103
06:59.280 --> 07:02.010
there are many factions among Sichuan warlords,

104
07:02.310 --> 07:03.600
and they are highly xenophobic.

105
07:03.490 --> 07:06.680
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Political Commissar of the Military Commission Column]

106
07:03.870 --> 07:07.160
It's hard for Chiang to dispatch troops from other provinces into Sichuan,

107
07:07.160 --> 07:10.270
and gives our army an advantage in mobile warfare.

108
07:14.660 --> 07:15.300
That's it?

109
07:15.420 --> 07:16.370
That's it.

110
07:17.510 --> 07:18.800
Does anyone disagree?

111
07:19.120 --> 07:19.680
Agreed.

112
07:19.720 --> 07:22.130
Agreed. Agreed.

113
07:22.480 --> 07:23.430
Right now,

114
07:23.630 --> 07:26.290
there's indeed no better strategic direction.

115
07:26.480 --> 07:27.280
Agreed.

116
07:27.800 --> 07:28.680
Comrade Enlai,

117
07:28.770 --> 07:30.610
do you have anything to add to this agenda?

118
07:30.610 --> 07:31.320
No.

119
07:33.630 --> 07:34.430
Alright then.

120
07:34.720 --> 07:37.000
Our first agenda is passed.

121
07:37.750 --> 07:40.040
Let's move on to today's second agenda.

122
07:40.430 --> 07:42.960
Firstly, on behalf of the Central Committee,

123
07:43.720 --> 07:45.950
regarding the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

124
07:45.950 --> 07:47.630
I will make a summary report.

125
08:17.070 --> 08:18.310
Comrades,

126
08:19.830 --> 08:21.690
before the formal report begins,

127
08:22.920 --> 08:24.920
I want to make one thing clear.

128
08:25.560 --> 08:28.120
Ever since I returned from Moscow Sun Yat-sen University

129
08:28.120 --> 08:30.040
and set foot on the motherland,

130
08:30.510 --> 08:31.680
I swore

131
08:32.240 --> 08:34.370
that for the communist cause of China,

132
08:34.440 --> 08:36.150
I would dedicate my all,

133
08:38.080 --> 08:39.600
including my life.

134
08:40.840 --> 08:41.789
Later,

135
08:42.080 --> 08:43.880
with Comrade Wang Ming's trust,

136
08:44.000 --> 08:45.000
he recommended me

137
08:45.120 --> 08:47.720
to be the head of the CPC Central Committee.

138
08:48.240 --> 08:49.030
I know

139
08:49.320 --> 08:51.510
with my age and seniority,

140
08:51.910 --> 08:54.480
it's difficult for me to take on this position.

141
08:54.480 --> 08:55.260
But at that time,

142
08:55.260 --> 08:56.260
I stepped up without hesitation

143
08:56.260 --> 08:58.120
and took on this responsibility.

144
08:58.390 --> 09:00.360
I want to say that no matter during this time

145
09:00.360 --> 09:02.060
[Kai Feng, He Kequan, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Central Representative in the 9th Red Army Corps]

146
09:00.600 --> 09:02.250
how much pressure I bore,

147
09:02.630 --> 09:05.200
I never forgot my original intention.

148
09:05.510 --> 09:07.720
I've spared no effort in following the Comintern

149
09:07.720 --> 09:09.510
and Comrade Wang Ming's instructions,

150
09:09.510 --> 09:12.000
earnestly executing strategic guidelines.

151
09:12.000 --> 09:12.910
In this regard,

152
09:13.150 --> 09:15.080
I have a clear conscience.

153
09:15.390 --> 09:15.650
I...

154
09:15.650 --> 09:16.450
Comrade Bo Gu,

155
09:16.800 --> 09:19.460
no one here questions your original intention.

156
09:19.870 --> 09:21.790
We'd rather hear

157
09:21.940 --> 09:24.480
your summary of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

158
09:24.480 --> 09:24.960
Yeah.

159
09:25.080 --> 09:25.670
Yeah.

160
09:49.810 --> 09:52.070
Our 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign

161
09:53.910 --> 09:55.550
has indeed failed,

162
09:55.840 --> 09:57.840
but the reasons are multi-faceted.

163
09:58.000 --> 09:59.150
The first point is

164
09:59.440 --> 10:00.360
that the imperialists

165
10:00.360 --> 10:03.030
and the Kuomintang reactionaries were too powerful.

166
10:03.030 --> 10:05.030
The Kuomintang mobilized 500,000 troops

167
10:05.030 --> 10:06.550
to besiege the Central Soviet Area.

168
10:06.550 --> 10:07.910
Plus other bases,

169
10:08.630 --> 10:10.720
their total strength reached one million.

170
10:10.720 --> 10:12.960
The disparity in strength was just too great.

171
10:12.960 --> 10:14.720
The disparity in weapons and equipment was even greater.

172
10:14.720 --> 10:17.320
They had 1,500 artillery pieces,

173
10:17.510 --> 10:18.840
and 500 aircraft.

174
10:19.150 --> 10:21.240
Moreover, due to the Kuomintang's long-term blockade

175
10:21.240 --> 10:22.360
of the Soviet Area,

176
10:23.090 --> 10:23.960
the Central Soviet Area's

177
10:23.960 --> 10:26.360
material supply was extremely difficult.

178
10:26.440 --> 10:28.040
Under these circumstances,

179
10:28.440 --> 10:30.150
it was hard for us to accumulate

180
10:30.150 --> 10:32.240
materials to fight a powerful enemy,

181
10:32.630 --> 10:34.120
as well as equipment supplies.

182
10:34.120 --> 10:35.000
Also,

183
10:34.370 --> 10:36.500
[Li Zhuoran, Political Commissar of the 5th Red Army Corps]

184
10:35.190 --> 10:36.310
our bases

185
10:37.120 --> 10:38.580
were divided by the enemy.

186
10:39.320 --> 10:41.120
Everyone fought independently,

187
10:41.120 --> 10:43.980
with insufficient coordination and cooperation.

188
10:44.120 --> 10:45.650
We were defeated one by one.

189
10:46.240 --> 10:47.910
This is also an objective reality.

190
10:47.910 --> 10:48.660
In addition,

191
10:49.120 --> 10:50.840
our work in the areas under Nationalist control

192
10:50.840 --> 10:52.970
has never made significant progress.

193
10:53.320 --> 10:56.600
The Party's mobilization of the masses in the areas under Nationalist control

194
10:56.600 --> 10:58.080
was not well carried out.

195
10:58.760 --> 11:00.480
Thus, they have never been able

196
10:59.900 --> 11:04.300
[Liu Shaoqi, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Central Representative in the 5th Red Army Corps]

197
11:00.510 --> 11:02.810
to effectively support the Central Soviet Area's

198
11:02.810 --> 11:04.810
Counter-Encirclement Campaigns.

199
11:05.000 --> 11:07.600
Also, as everyone knows,

200
11:07.910 --> 11:10.320
during the Nationalists' 5th Encirclement Campaign,

201
11:10.320 --> 11:12.380
they adopted new strategic tactics,

202
11:12.720 --> 11:14.320
relying on blockhouse warfare

203
11:14.320 --> 11:16.670
to steadily constrict our Central Soviet Area.

204
11:16.670 --> 11:18.960
However, our tactic of blockhouse against blockhouse

205
11:18.960 --> 11:21.600
was never properly implemented and executed.

206
11:38.670 --> 11:39.550
In short,

207
11:39.590 --> 11:41.530
these insurmountable difficulties

208
11:41.530 --> 11:43.930
directly or indirectly led to

209
11:43.960 --> 11:46.020
the failure of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

210
11:46.020 --> 11:48.900
As a result, we lost many comrades.

211
11:49.480 --> 11:51.440
As the person in overall charge of the Central Committee,

212
11:51.440 --> 11:54.080
I feel very guilty and blame myself.

213
11:54.750 --> 11:55.960
I am deeply pained.

214
11:56.510 --> 11:58.150
I have let our comrades down.

215
12:04.740 --> 12:05.620
Comrade Bo Gu,

216
12:06.150 --> 12:09.870
is your main report finished?

217
12:10.550 --> 12:11.520
Yes.

218
12:12.270 --> 12:13.390
Is that all?

219
12:13.600 --> 12:14.760
That's all.

220
12:15.360 --> 12:18.600
Of course, we can discuss it together.

221
12:19.120 --> 12:20.240
Comrade Bo Gu,

222
12:20.910 --> 12:22.720
besides the objective reasons

223
12:23.240 --> 12:24.390
you just mentioned,

224
12:24.520 --> 12:27.560
were there any subjective mistakes?

225
12:29.910 --> 12:30.790
Of course.

226
12:31.440 --> 12:34.030
The Central Committee underestimated the difficulties

227
12:34.030 --> 12:35.240
of the Counter-Encirclement Campaigns,

228
12:35.240 --> 12:37.770
so during specific command implementation,

229
12:37.790 --> 12:39.550
there were indeed some mistakes.

230
12:39.550 --> 12:40.790
Comrade Bo Gu,

231
12:40.950 --> 12:43.280
when you talked about objective reasons,

232
12:43.630 --> 12:46.320
you spoke at such length.

233
12:46.870 --> 12:49.960
Why is it that when it comes to subjective mistakes

234
12:49.960 --> 12:51.160
in military command,

235
12:51.550 --> 12:53.410
you are so sparing with your words

236
12:53.430 --> 12:54.690
and just brush over it?

237
12:54.890 --> 12:57.440
Were there merely some mistakes?

238
12:57.910 --> 13:00.840
Was there no problem with the overall military line

239
13:01.240 --> 13:02.720
you led?

240
13:03.000 --> 13:04.440
The military line of the Central Committee

241
13:04.440 --> 13:06.320
was approved by the Comintern.

242
13:06.630 --> 13:08.030
What is there to question?

243
13:08.030 --> 13:09.790
Is what the Comintern approved

244
13:10.150 --> 13:12.030
always correct?

245
13:12.390 --> 13:14.270
Even if it was correct at the time,

246
13:14.510 --> 13:16.600
with the changes in the military situation,

247
13:16.600 --> 13:18.570
should we rigidly stick to it

248
13:18.600 --> 13:20.000
without adapting?

249
13:20.020 --> 13:21.080
Comrade Jiaxiang,

250
13:21.090 --> 13:22.850
we did not rigidly stick to it.

251
13:23.240 --> 13:24.960
Otherwise, how could we have made

252
13:24.960 --> 13:26.790
the decision for a strategic transfer?

253
13:26.790 --> 13:28.600
Moreover, just now,

254
13:28.840 --> 13:29.720
everyone agreed

255
13:29.720 --> 13:31.200
on the new strategic direction

256
13:31.200 --> 13:33.030
of establishing a base area in northwestern Sichuan.

257
13:33.030 --> 13:34.720
Aren't these all adaptations?

258
13:34.720 --> 13:36.450
After the strategic transfer,

259
13:36.510 --> 13:37.630
you clearly saw

260
13:38.000 --> 13:40.400
the enemy had set up several defense lines,

261
13:40.440 --> 13:43.240
but you still insisted on going down a blind alley,

262
13:43.390 --> 13:44.790
not knowing how to adapt.

263
13:45.080 --> 13:46.550
Now that the enemy has blockade lines,

264
13:46.550 --> 13:48.000
do we just stop moving?

265
13:48.360 --> 13:50.220
Wouldn't that become flightism?

266
13:50.550 --> 13:51.240
Besides,

267
13:51.480 --> 13:52.870
the direction of the strategic transfer

268
13:52.870 --> 13:54.790
was approved by the Comintern.

269
13:55.080 --> 13:57.720
We clearly had a better route to take.

270
13:58.120 --> 14:01.720
How can that be called flightism?

271
14:02.210 --> 14:03.970
If we have a better route,

272
14:04.000 --> 14:06.150
why can't it be implemented?

273
14:06.600 --> 14:08.750
Take the excellent suggestions

274
14:09.080 --> 14:11.080
proposed by Comrade Mao Zedong,

275
14:11.270 --> 14:13.600
why couldn't we give them a try?

276
14:13.620 --> 14:15.630
If Mao Zedong's suggestions haven't been tried,

277
14:15.630 --> 14:17.220
how do you know they are correct?

278
14:17.220 --> 14:18.420
But facts have proven

279
14:18.630 --> 14:20.750
that Mao's opinions are correct.

280
14:20.910 --> 14:22.000
How are they proven?

281
14:22.000 --> 14:24.130
What basis do you have for saying that?

282
14:24.150 --> 14:25.910
Are you relying on your narrow empiricism?

283
14:25.910 --> 14:26.740
How is it narrow?

284
14:26.740 --> 14:27.790
What do you mean by narrow empiricism?

285
14:27.790 --> 14:30.390
These experiences were bought with our lives!

286
14:30.390 --> 14:31.630
How can you say that?

287
14:33.120 --> 14:34.520
Let's present the facts.

288
14:36.250 --> 14:37.460
Comrades,

289
14:38.120 --> 14:41.320
I will now give the supplementary report of this meeting.

290
14:42.150 --> 14:44.080
Comrade Bo Gu, may I begin?

291
14:44.720 --> 14:45.790
Of course.

292
14:46.120 --> 14:48.030
Regarding the summary of military affairs,

293
14:48.030 --> 14:49.630
Comrade Enlai is an expert.

294
14:50.080 --> 14:51.670
His words are authoritative.

295
14:51.670 --> 14:54.160
Let's invite Comrade Enlai to give the report.

296
14:54.160 --> 14:56.360
Everyone, please listen to the speech.

297
14:59.370 --> 15:00.350
I believe

298
15:01.550 --> 15:03.150
the main reason for the failure

299
15:03.150 --> 15:05.550
of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign

300
15:05.870 --> 15:08.670
lies in the strategies and tactics we formulated.

301
15:09.200 --> 15:10.910
There were serious mistakes.

302
15:12.750 --> 15:15.390
The Kuomintang's

303
15:15.390 --> 15:16.720
5th Encirclement against the Central Soviet Area

304
15:16.720 --> 15:19.200
started in late September 1933.

305
15:19.440 --> 15:21.770
Unlike the previous four Encirclements,

306
15:21.790 --> 15:23.030
this time,

307
15:23.630 --> 15:26.200
the enemy adopted blockhouse tactics,

308
15:26.670 --> 15:29.520
squeezing the Central Soviet Area step by step.

309
15:30.720 --> 15:32.030
But we formulated

310
15:32.060 --> 15:34.660
a strategy of keeping the enemy outside the gates

311
15:34.660 --> 15:36.170
and engaging in blockhouse warfare

312
15:36.170 --> 15:37.650
with a powerful enemy.

313
15:38.440 --> 15:41.960
As a result, the Red Army Corps completely lost

314
15:41.960 --> 15:43.910
the tactical advantage of flexibility

315
15:43.910 --> 15:46.200
we had in the previous four counter-campaigns.

316
15:46.200 --> 15:48.770
This shows that our strategy and tactics

317
15:48.800 --> 15:49.770
were wrong.

318
15:53.120 --> 15:53.790
Zhou,

319
15:53.900 --> 15:58.570
is this your criticism of me and Comrade Bo Gu?

320
15:58.950 --> 16:01.750
Comrade Li De, what you said is not comprehensive.

321
16:01.910 --> 16:04.120
As one of the formulators and executors

322
16:04.550 --> 16:06.080
of the wrong military strategies,

323
16:06.080 --> 16:07.480
I was the one who agreed to

324
16:07.510 --> 16:09.910
the blockhouse against blockhouse combat plan,

325
16:09.910 --> 16:12.390
and the full-scale resistance of six routes against six routes.

326
16:12.390 --> 16:14.390
Including a series of military commands

327
16:14.390 --> 16:16.120
since the strategic transfer,

328
16:16.350 --> 16:18.380
I was involved in making the decisions.

329
16:18.380 --> 16:20.470
The vast majority of the strategic deployments

330
16:20.470 --> 16:22.780
were implemented by me.

331
16:23.390 --> 16:26.270
I bear a heavy responsibility for these mistakes.

332
16:26.790 --> 16:29.120
I will admit my own faults.

333
16:30.230 --> 16:32.130
I implore the organization to deal with my mistakes

334
16:32.130 --> 16:33.800
seriously.

335
16:34.750 --> 16:35.750
I am willing to accept

336
16:35.750 --> 16:38.150
any punishment the organization gives me.

337
16:39.090 --> 16:40.420
Speaking of criticism,

338
16:41.080 --> 16:42.270
what I want to criticize

339
16:42.270 --> 16:44.670
is everyone who led to the wrong line.

340
16:46.000 --> 16:46.960
Comrade Bo Gu,

341
16:47.360 --> 16:48.320
Comrade Li De,

342
16:48.650 --> 16:50.810
wrong is wrong.

343
16:51.390 --> 16:52.390
I hope you will

344
16:52.830 --> 16:54.470
admit your own faults too.

345
16:55.360 --> 16:57.680
The night before the strategic transfer,

346
16:57.680 --> 17:00.040
a messenger soldier named Chen Xinbiao

347
17:00.440 --> 17:01.720
asked me a question

348
17:01.750 --> 17:03.550
when he came to deliver a letter.

349
17:03.950 --> 17:05.150
"Vice Chairman Zhou,

350
17:05.200 --> 17:06.349
where are we going?

351
17:07.180 --> 17:08.869
Will we ever come back?"

352
17:09.109 --> 17:11.170
Facing a fifteen-year-old comrade,

353
17:11.200 --> 17:12.640
I thought for a long time

354
17:14.000 --> 17:15.069
and had no answer.

355
17:15.550 --> 17:16.790
I could only tell him,

356
17:17.550 --> 17:19.500
Chen Xinbiao, I'm sorry,

357
17:19.790 --> 17:21.990
I can't answer your question right now.

358
17:22.079 --> 17:23.690
Please give me some time,

359
17:24.480 --> 17:26.540
I will definitely give you an answer.

360
17:27.550 --> 17:28.750
More than a month ago,

361
17:29.500 --> 17:31.300
fifteen-year-old Chen Xinbiao

362
17:33.160 --> 17:35.360
sacrificed his life by the Xiang River.

363
17:35.390 --> 17:36.350
I know

364
17:37.350 --> 17:38.520
there are many other comrades

365
17:38.520 --> 17:40.640
who have the same question in their hearts.

366
17:40.640 --> 17:42.640
Until they sacrificed their lives,

367
17:42.720 --> 17:44.530
they didn't get an answer either.

368
17:44.530 --> 17:46.680
[Deng Fa, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Director of the National Political Defense Bureau]

369
17:44.960 --> 17:45.690
If a comrade

370
17:46.160 --> 17:48.790
asks me the same question today,

371
17:48.960 --> 17:50.310
do I

372
17:51.550 --> 17:53.640
still have no answer?

373
17:56.290 --> 17:58.420
I only hope that a meeting like today

374
17:59.050 --> 18:01.010
can give all comrades

375
18:01.300 --> 18:02.990
a fair answer.

376
18:06.000 --> 18:07.310
My report is finished.

377
18:24.090 --> 18:26.440
I think Comrade Zhou Enlai's report

378
18:27.640 --> 18:28.640
is objective,

379
18:28.750 --> 18:29.840
factual,

380
18:30.350 --> 18:31.400
and sincere.

381
18:31.720 --> 18:32.590
In contrast,

382
18:32.960 --> 18:34.270
Comrade Bo Gu's report

383
18:34.790 --> 18:37.590
is evasive and shirks responsibility.

384
18:37.830 --> 18:39.830
I don't agree with Comrade Bo Gu's report.

385
18:39.830 --> 18:41.240
Well said, Jiaxiang.

386
18:41.550 --> 18:42.720
I don't agree either.

387
18:42.720 --> 18:43.790
Disagree. Disagree.

388
18:43.790 --> 18:45.480
Your speech is just evasive.

389
18:45.880 --> 18:46.880
Since we're having this meeting,

390
18:46.880 --> 18:47.970
why beat around the bush?

391
18:47.970 --> 18:50.030
If you want to beat around the bush, don't hold this meeting!

392
18:50.030 --> 18:51.890
So many frontline soldiers died.

393
18:52.400 --> 18:53.970
Who will pay for this?

394
18:54.110 --> 18:55.550
So many soldiers died.

395
18:55.830 --> 18:57.430
Can a single "wrong command"

396
18:57.440 --> 18:58.640
just end it hastily?

397
18:58.680 --> 19:00.280
What are you all trying to do?

398
19:01.350 --> 19:02.880
The topic of our meeting now

399
19:03.640 --> 19:05.170
is to summarize the lessons

400
19:05.750 --> 19:08.090
of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign and the strategic transfer.

401
19:08.090 --> 19:10.200
I already admitted in my report just now

402
19:10.200 --> 19:11.070
that we failed

403
19:11.070 --> 19:12.210
the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

404
19:12.210 --> 19:13.550
I discussed the objective causes,

405
19:13.550 --> 19:14.510
and the subjective causes

406
19:14.510 --> 19:16.910
were mentioned in Comrade Enlai's report.

407
19:17.030 --> 19:18.030
What else can be done?

408
19:18.030 --> 19:18.750
I believe

409
19:18.990 --> 19:21.120
the reports of Comrades Bo Gu and Enlai

410
19:21.350 --> 19:23.230
are comprehensive when combined.

411
19:23.230 --> 19:25.750
Enlai put it well in his speech just now.

412
19:26.270 --> 19:28.110
You have to pay the piper.

413
19:28.300 --> 19:28.860
Exactly.

414
19:28.970 --> 19:29.900
We need an explanation.

415
19:29.900 --> 19:30.750
Who will step forward?

416
19:30.750 --> 19:32.410
Mind the meeting discipline.

417
19:32.720 --> 19:35.250
This is an enlarged meeting of the Politburo.

418
19:35.580 --> 19:37.110
Everyone, watch your tone.

419
19:37.110 --> 19:38.040
What do you mean?

420
19:38.350 --> 19:40.880
We were called here to speak our minds freely.

421
19:41.070 --> 19:42.810
Otherwise, we shouldn't have come.

422
19:42.740 --> 19:45.500
[Li Fuchun, Acting Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

423
19:42.830 --> 19:44.430
This is an enlarged meeting.

424
19:44.450 --> 19:45.840
Everyone should be allowed to speak.

425
19:45.690 --> 19:47.780
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

426
19:46.180 --> 19:47.180
Comrade Kai Feng,

427
19:47.830 --> 19:49.030
if you don't let us speak,

428
19:49.030 --> 19:51.310
why are we here?

429
19:51.590 --> 19:52.200
Exactly.

430
19:52.440 --> 19:54.230
If you won't let us express our opinions,

431
19:54.230 --> 19:56.040
then what's the point

432
19:56.070 --> 19:57.450
of this Politburo enlarged meeting?

433
19:57.450 --> 19:58.550
Since it's an enlarged meeting,

434
19:58.550 --> 20:00.540
everyone gets a say

435
20:00.590 --> 20:02.000
to express what's on their mind.

436
20:02.000 --> 20:02.460
Indeed.

437
20:02.640 --> 20:03.770
Comrades,

438
20:04.090 --> 20:05.620
we are holding this meeting

439
20:06.200 --> 20:08.410
to discuss issues frankly and openly.

440
20:09.000 --> 20:11.400
I believe everyone can speak freely.

441
20:14.270 --> 20:17.350
Mao, it's your turn to speak.

442
20:17.850 --> 20:19.580
You are the main character now.

443
20:19.720 --> 20:20.720
What is he saying?

444
20:25.530 --> 20:27.250
Mao, it's your turn to speak.

445
20:27.460 --> 20:29.190
You are the main character now.

446
20:38.580 --> 20:40.890
Comrades, I'll share my views.

447
20:47.370 --> 20:48.410
I think

448
20:49.440 --> 20:50.830
Comrade Bo Gu's report

449
20:51.130 --> 20:53.930
is fundamentally incorrect.

450
20:59.220 --> 21:01.410
Do those of us here remember

451
21:02.220 --> 21:04.380
that in 1930, Comrade Zedong

452
21:04.880 --> 21:05.920
wrote an article

453
21:06.440 --> 21:08.400
called Work of Investigation?

454
21:08.790 --> 21:11.680
That was truly prescient.

455
21:12.550 --> 21:13.400
It said

456
21:13.720 --> 21:15.750
that many of our newly appointed cadres

457
21:15.750 --> 21:18.550
like to announce their political views as soon as they arrive.

458
21:18.550 --> 21:21.060
Upon seeing a little surface detail, a minor branch,

459
21:21.060 --> 21:22.640
they start pointing fingers

460
21:22.640 --> 21:24.850
and spouting pure subjective nonsense.

461
21:24.850 --> 21:25.770
They think

462
21:26.090 --> 21:27.760
that following what's in the books

463
21:27.760 --> 21:30.140
and doing things based on others' experiences

464
21:30.140 --> 21:31.900
will always lead to victory.

465
21:32.420 --> 21:33.520
Is that really so?

466
21:34.240 --> 21:35.280
Comrade Bo Gu,

467
21:36.160 --> 21:37.480
your report just now

468
21:37.920 --> 21:40.640
overemphasized the objective difficulties.

469
21:40.930 --> 21:44.330
But regarding your own subjective errors in understanding,

470
21:44.480 --> 21:45.730
you avoided the topic entirely.

471
21:45.730 --> 21:47.590
This is irresponsible behavior,

472
21:47.740 --> 21:48.910
and entirely wrong.

473
21:49.550 --> 21:50.940
On the contrary, I believe

474
21:50.940 --> 21:53.920
that the failure of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign

475
21:53.920 --> 21:57.120
and our repeated setbacks during the strategic transfer

476
21:57.270 --> 22:00.630
were caused far more by subjective errors than by objective conditions.

477
22:00.630 --> 22:02.110
After the Counter-Encirclement Campaign began,

478
22:02.110 --> 22:04.370
the leadership of Comrades Bo Gu and Li De

479
22:04.810 --> 22:06.530
was extremely undemocratic.

480
22:07.270 --> 22:09.810
All work of the Military Commission has always been

481
22:09.810 --> 22:13.050
practically monopolized by Comrade Li De alone.

482
22:13.540 --> 22:15.360
The Military Commission's collective leadership power

483
22:15.360 --> 22:16.790
was completely abolished.

484
22:16.790 --> 22:18.590
Punitive measures ran rampant,

485
22:18.640 --> 22:20.510
and there was absolutely no self-criticism.

486
22:20.510 --> 22:22.240
Towards all opposing views,

487
22:22.780 --> 22:24.490
you not only completely ignored them,

488
22:24.490 --> 22:27.750
but also took various suppressive and punitive measures.

489
22:27.920 --> 22:29.440
You even went so far as to

490
22:29.670 --> 22:31.550
deliberately marginalize and suppress

491
22:31.550 --> 22:33.920
comrades holding different opinions.

492
22:34.350 --> 22:36.580
How is this anywhere close to being democratic?

493
22:36.580 --> 22:39.380
How is there any organizational discipline left?

494
22:39.880 --> 22:41.090
All of the above

495
22:41.880 --> 22:45.810
created highly abnormal conditions within the Military Commission.

496
22:46.750 --> 22:48.740
Comrade Stalin said, in his

497
22:49.130 --> 22:51.130
"Foundations of Leninism",

498
22:51.520 --> 22:53.790
that theory divorced from revolutionary practice

499
22:53.790 --> 22:55.220
is empty theory,

500
22:55.310 --> 22:58.040
and practice not guided by revolutionary theory

501
22:58.070 --> 22:59.440
is blind practice.

502
23:00.030 --> 23:01.920
I think Comrade Bo Gu

503
23:02.310 --> 23:05.040
just applied empty theories

504
23:05.070 --> 23:06.720
completely divorced from practice

505
23:06.720 --> 23:08.590
to blindly guide practice.

506
23:09.110 --> 23:10.110
The final result,

507
23:10.480 --> 23:12.480
in Comrade Zedong's words,

508
23:12.830 --> 23:14.790
is making a serious

509
23:15.080 --> 23:16.380
bookish mistake.

510
23:16.400 --> 23:17.430
Comrade Luofu,

511
23:17.670 --> 23:19.500
I admit we had some flaws

512
23:19.530 --> 23:20.530
in our work,

513
23:20.960 --> 23:22.270
but you blame all the mistakes

514
23:22.270 --> 23:23.930
on Comrade Li De and me.

515
23:23.960 --> 23:24.720
Is that fair?

516
23:24.740 --> 23:26.360
Is shirking responsibility fair?

517
23:26.360 --> 23:28.270
At the start of the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

518
23:28.270 --> 23:29.720
you blamed the fall of Lichuan

519
23:29.720 --> 23:31.030
and the defeat at Huwan

520
23:31.120 --> 23:32.650
entirely on Xiao Jinguang,

521
23:32.850 --> 23:33.810
but you never mentioned a word about

522
23:33.810 --> 23:35.960
your own chaotic and blind command.

523
23:36.450 --> 23:37.710
The KMT 19th Route Army

524
23:37.790 --> 23:39.520
launched the Fujian Incident.

525
23:39.930 --> 23:41.830
You ignored Comrade Zedong's proposal

526
23:41.830 --> 23:44.070
to form a united front with them

527
23:44.300 --> 23:47.070
and strike outward to annihilate the enemy.

528
23:47.400 --> 23:48.830
You turned a deaf ear to it,

529
23:48.830 --> 23:49.880
making us lose

530
23:50.260 --> 23:51.300
a perfect opportunity

531
23:51.300 --> 23:52.610
to break the 5th encirclement

532
23:52.610 --> 23:53.850
from the outside.

533
23:54.480 --> 23:55.680
In the Battle of Guangchang,

534
23:55.680 --> 23:58.550
you and Li De set up a field headquarters,

535
23:58.830 --> 24:00.290
monopolized the command,

536
24:00.390 --> 24:03.200
and defended Guangchang, which had no natural defense.

537
24:03.200 --> 24:06.120
You rejected so many comrades' suggestions.

538
24:06.440 --> 24:07.300
And the result?

539
24:07.750 --> 24:12.270
Guangchang, the northern gate of the Soviet Area, was lost.

540
24:13.370 --> 24:15.680
The enemy's encirclement kept shrinking.

541
24:15.680 --> 24:17.080
Comrade Zedong proposed

542
24:17.270 --> 24:19.530
to push the main force into central Hunan

543
24:19.530 --> 24:20.790
and fight on the outer lines.

544
24:20.790 --> 24:22.200
You still wouldn't listen.

545
24:22.200 --> 24:24.200
Instead, you divided our forces into six routes

546
24:24.200 --> 24:25.640
to resist the enemy separately.

547
24:25.640 --> 24:27.680
This led to our continuous defeats,

548
24:28.160 --> 24:29.640
and finally we had to

549
24:29.880 --> 24:31.680
abandon our Central Soviet Area

550
24:31.760 --> 24:34.330
and were forced to begin the strategic shift.

551
24:35.110 --> 24:36.710
During the strategic shift,

552
24:37.380 --> 24:39.420
Comrade Zedong made multiple suggestions

553
24:39.420 --> 24:41.640
on the marching route and strategic direction.

554
24:41.640 --> 24:42.770
And you?

555
24:43.050 --> 24:44.570
You turned a deaf ear.

556
24:44.960 --> 24:46.930
You mechanically, stubbornly,

557
24:46.960 --> 24:49.370
and rigidly stuck to the plan

558
24:49.400 --> 24:50.960
made before departure.

559
24:51.590 --> 24:53.680
This resulted in our route and direction

560
24:53.680 --> 24:56.610
being completely predicted by the enemy.

561
24:57.290 --> 24:58.090
And we?

562
24:58.370 --> 25:00.850
We could only watch our entire force

563
25:01.200 --> 25:03.920
march right into the enemy's pocket trap

564
25:04.120 --> 25:05.920
at the Xiang River.

565
25:06.460 --> 25:10.190
Tens of thousands of Red Army soldiers suffered heavy casualties.

566
25:10.330 --> 25:13.360
For this series of failures and losses,

567
25:14.790 --> 25:18.480
can you shirk your responsibilities?

568
25:21.560 --> 25:22.370
Well said!

569
25:33.890 --> 25:35.450
I'm done speaking.

570
25:39.290 --> 25:41.290
I'd like to express my opinion.

571
25:43.260 --> 25:44.990
I want to speak.

572
25:45.880 --> 25:48.160
Comrade Li De, as a non-voting delegate,

573
25:48.630 --> 25:50.550
you certainly have the right to speak.

574
25:50.550 --> 25:51.960
I completely and firmly disagree

575
25:51.960 --> 25:54.750
with your criticism of me.

576
25:54.770 --> 25:55.970
As a military advisor

577
25:56.480 --> 25:58.340
sent to China by the Comintern,

578
25:58.400 --> 26:01.680
I've always been fulfilling my duties.

579
26:01.700 --> 26:04.110
I've been using the advanced military theories

580
26:04.110 --> 26:06.720
I am familiar with,

581
26:07.030 --> 26:11.030
as well as the successful war experience of the Soviet Union,

582
26:11.030 --> 26:13.110
to help you.

583
26:26.880 --> 26:29.930
Yet you all see the result.

584
26:30.300 --> 26:31.860
Yet you all see the result.

585
26:31.890 --> 26:32.660
Li De!

586
26:39.180 --> 26:40.530
Your excuses

587
26:41.180 --> 26:42.420
are nothing new.

588
26:43.630 --> 26:44.670
Comrade Li De,

589
26:45.350 --> 26:46.550
even now,

590
26:46.980 --> 26:49.550
you're still shirking responsibility.

591
26:51.560 --> 26:54.600
No, I am not shirking responsibility.

592
26:55.260 --> 26:56.300
Listen to me.

593
26:57.640 --> 26:59.030
I came to China

594
26:59.030 --> 27:01.440
not to ruin this army.

595
27:01.910 --> 27:02.950
I came here

596
27:03.110 --> 27:07.440
to lead this army to victory.

597
27:07.720 --> 27:09.810
I've always been with this army.

598
27:09.830 --> 27:12.420
I'm not afraid of sacrifice.

599
27:12.910 --> 27:13.830
Do you think such heavy casualties

600
27:13.830 --> 27:14.700
are easy for me?

601
27:15.360 --> 27:16.640
Do you think such heavy casualties

602
27:16.640 --> 27:17.510
are easy for me?

603
27:18.160 --> 27:19.720
Do you think seeing such heavy casualties

604
27:19.720 --> 27:20.590
isn't painful for me?

605
27:20.590 --> 27:22.180
Do you think seeing such heavy casualties

606
27:22.180 --> 27:23.370
isn't painful for me?

607
27:23.370 --> 27:26.050
Do you think I can sleep soundly?

608
27:26.350 --> 27:28.150
Do you think I can sleep soundly?

609
27:29.030 --> 27:31.920
I've been thinking,

610
27:31.920 --> 27:33.480
why is it like this?

611
27:33.480 --> 27:34.640
I've been thinking,

612
27:35.400 --> 27:36.400
why is it like this?

613
27:36.400 --> 27:37.830
Where did it go wrong?

614
27:38.220 --> 27:41.180
Why can't such advanced Soviet theories

615
27:41.200 --> 27:45.720
be applied in China?

616
27:46.020 --> 27:48.340
Whose fault is this?

617
27:48.790 --> 27:51.620
Is it the Soviet Union's?

618
27:52.860 --> 27:55.420
Or is it mine?

619
27:56.310 --> 27:58.750
It's your fault.

620
27:59.680 --> 28:01.900
You haven't mastered advanced military skills,

621
28:01.900 --> 28:04.750
so you can't execute the battle plans.

622
28:04.800 --> 28:08.150
You are not ready to sacrifice.

623
28:08.680 --> 28:10.850
You haven't mastered advanced military skills,

624
28:10.850 --> 28:12.720
so you can't execute the battle plans.

625
28:12.720 --> 28:14.340
Most importantly,

626
28:14.370 --> 28:16.410
you are not ready to sacrifice,

627
28:16.720 --> 28:19.200
