But sooner or later,

644
29:03.660 --> 29:04.980
we will eventually

645
29:05.000 --> 29:08.920
re-establish contact with the Comintern.

646
29:09.240 --> 29:10.440
When that time comes,

647
29:10.550 --> 29:11.500
you will all be held responsible

648
29:11.500 --> 29:12.560
for your mistakes.

649
29:19.050 --> 29:20.650
I'd like to ask Comrade Li De,

650
29:20.970 --> 29:23.540
how far is Moscow from Zunyi?

651
29:25.120 --> 29:25.840
Translate.

652
29:26.200 --> 29:28.880
How far is Moscow from Zunyi?

653
29:29.110 --> 29:30.510
How far is Red Square in Moscow

654
29:30.510 --> 29:32.430
from the parade ground in Ruijin?

655
29:37.200 --> 29:38.330
Comrade Mao Zedong,

656
29:38.690 --> 29:39.800
are you saying

657
29:39.830 --> 29:42.020
the successful Soviet revolution experience is useless?

658
29:42.020 --> 29:43.820
Do you want to do things your way?

659
29:43.910 --> 29:46.770
Comrade Kai Feng, don't take things out of context.

660
29:47.270 --> 29:48.980
The successful Soviet revolution experience

661
29:48.980 --> 29:50.840
was won with blood and sacrifice.

662
29:50.850 --> 29:52.850
We should respect and learn from it.

663
29:53.500 --> 29:54.830
But we must also respect

664
29:54.990 --> 29:56.470
our own experiences.

665
29:57.070 --> 29:57.800
What's more,

666
29:58.040 --> 30:00.630
our experiences came at such a painful cost.

667
30:07.600 --> 30:08.460
Comrades,

668
30:09.710 --> 30:12.470
this is a detailed report I asked the Operations Bureau to compile

669
30:12.470 --> 30:14.040
on the major battles since

670
30:14.330 --> 30:16.660
the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

671
30:17.620 --> 30:20.310
April 1934, the Battle of Guangchang

672
30:20.830 --> 30:21.960
lasted 18 days.

673
30:22.070 --> 30:25.310
The Red Army suffered 5,093 casualties,

674
30:25.830 --> 30:28.640
about a quarter of the total combatants.

675
30:29.270 --> 30:30.680
Among them, the 3rd Red Army Corps

676
30:30.680 --> 30:32.590
suffered 2,705 casualties.

677
30:32.960 --> 30:35.270
The Political Director of the 6th Red Division,

678
30:35.270 --> 30:37.530
Comrade Cao Qican, sacrificed his life.

679
30:37.600 --> 30:38.330
In August,

680
30:38.550 --> 30:41.210
the positional defense battle north of Yiqian,

681
30:41.400 --> 30:43.640
the Red Army suffered over 2,300 casualties,

682
30:43.640 --> 30:46.640
including over 600 officers.

683
30:49.150 --> 30:49.950
In September,

684
30:50.400 --> 30:52.420
at Songmaoling in Changting, Fujian,

685
30:52.420 --> 30:53.940
in order to cover the strategic shift of the Central Red Army,

686
30:53.940 --> 30:55.930
the commanders and fighters of the 9th Red Army Corps

687
30:55.930 --> 30:58.200
and the 24th Red Division

688
30:58.750 --> 31:00.260
celebrated the Mid-Autumn Festival in advance

689
31:00.260 --> 31:02.940
on September 22nd,

690
31:04.020 --> 31:06.150
the 14th day of the eighth lunar month.

691
31:06.440 --> 31:08.240
Because starting from the 15th,

692
31:08.720 --> 31:11.350
they fought a bloody battle for seven days and nights

693
31:11.350 --> 31:13.750
against an enemy several times their size.

694
31:13.840 --> 31:15.700
Comrade Luo Binghui told me later

695
31:15.810 --> 31:19.000
there was a bridge in Zhongwu Village behind the front line.

696
31:19.000 --> 31:20.690
There was a conscription office there.

697
31:20.690 --> 31:22.490
A line was drawn on a wooden post.

698
31:22.990 --> 31:25.840
It was the height of a Hanyang-made rifle.

699
31:26.320 --> 31:28.950
As long as one was taller than that height,

700
31:29.270 --> 31:30.670
they could join the army.

701
31:30.920 --> 31:32.950
Many kids wanted to go to the battlefield

702
31:32.950 --> 31:35.010
and stood on their tiptoes to enlist.

703
31:35.940 --> 31:37.120
They charged into battle

704
31:37.120 --> 31:39.920
with spears and machetes.

705
31:41.000 --> 31:42.460
For seven days and nights,

706
31:42.790 --> 31:44.850
thousands of young Red Army soldiers

707
31:45.030 --> 31:46.110
died there.

708
31:46.430 --> 31:48.690
Before they died, many soldiers

709
31:48.950 --> 31:50.640
reached into their pockets.

710
31:51.350 --> 31:52.750
Because in their pockets

711
31:52.800 --> 31:55.860
were mooncakes they hadn't brought themselves to eat.

712
31:56.650 --> 31:58.970
When many soldiers died,

713
32:01.640 --> 32:03.260
half the mooncake was swallowed

714
32:03.260 --> 32:05.720
and the other half was still in their mouths.

715
32:15.780 --> 32:17.440
After the strategic retreat,

716
32:18.530 --> 32:21.050
we continuously broke through the enemy's blockade.

717
32:21.050 --> 32:22.440
At the first blockade,

718
32:23.260 --> 32:25.790
the Red Army suffered over 3,700 casualties.

719
32:26.110 --> 32:29.130
Hong Chao, Commander of the 4th Division, died in action.

720
32:29.130 --> 32:30.460
At the second blockade,

721
32:30.510 --> 32:32.430
the Red Army suffered over 9,700 casualties.

722
32:32.430 --> 32:33.690
At the third blockade,

723
32:33.920 --> 32:36.350
the Red Army suffered over 8,600 casualties.

724
32:36.350 --> 32:38.150
Over a month ago at the Xiang River,

725
32:38.150 --> 32:39.750
after five days and nights of fierce fighting,

726
32:39.750 --> 32:42.270
our Red Army was reduced from over 80,000 men

727
32:42.590 --> 32:45.000
to just over 30,000.

728
32:46.180 --> 32:47.980
Blood stained the clear waters.

729
32:48.980 --> 32:51.110
The river was full of floating bodies.

730
32:51.820 --> 32:54.340
How many of our excellent cadres

731
32:54.830 --> 32:58.270
and young Red Army soldiers are there?

732
32:59.150 --> 33:00.150
Chen Shuxiang...

733
33:00.510 --> 33:02.030
I gave him that name.

734
33:02.600 --> 33:04.880
In 1921, at Qingshuitang in Changsha,

735
33:05.310 --> 33:06.510
when I first met him,

736
33:07.310 --> 33:08.680
he was only this tall.

737
33:09.960 --> 33:10.880
He was 16.

738
33:11.200 --> 33:12.480
Every day he would carry a load on a shoulder pole,

739
33:12.480 --> 33:14.600
crossing a ridge to deliver vegetables.

740
33:14.600 --> 33:15.710
One day on the road,

741
33:16.000 --> 33:17.530
a bramble pricked his foot.

742
33:17.830 --> 33:18.750
The teenager

743
33:19.030 --> 33:20.690
was crying loudly on the road,

744
33:21.000 --> 33:22.830
saying he was afraid of pain since he was a kid.

745
33:22.830 --> 33:24.360
Later I put medicine on him.

746
33:24.550 --> 33:26.480
He just sat on his vegetable basket

747
33:26.830 --> 33:28.230
listening to my lecture.

748
33:28.360 --> 33:30.840
Once he listened, he was unstoppable.

749
33:31.440 --> 33:32.840
It's been over ten years.

750
33:33.000 --> 33:35.440
That kid who was only this tall

751
33:35.660 --> 33:37.910
has grown into a hero.

752
33:38.440 --> 33:40.640
A kid who was afraid of pain since childhood,

753
33:40.640 --> 33:44.200
forcefully tore his own intestines apart,

754
33:44.430 --> 33:46.090
rather than become a captive.

755
33:46.140 --> 33:47.170
These days,

756
33:47.610 --> 33:50.670
my mind is full of that kid at Qingshuitang in Changsha,

757
33:51.220 --> 33:54.020
sitting on his vegetable basket,

758
33:54.720 --> 33:57.210
listening to my lecture.

759
33:58.690 --> 34:00.610
Did Moscow see these sacrifices?

760
34:01.310 --> 34:02.330
Does Moscow wants to see

761
34:02.330 --> 34:04.250
these sacrifices?

762
34:04.740 --> 34:06.130
Absolutely not.

763
34:07.010 --> 34:08.230
Which of our sacrificed comrades,

764
34:08.230 --> 34:09.719
and comrades who are still alive,

765
34:09.719 --> 34:11.199
is afraid of death?

766
34:12.600 --> 34:14.600
We can fight to the death to survive,

767
34:14.610 --> 34:17.540
but we absolutely cannot just die for no good reason.

768
34:17.850 --> 34:20.400
A wrong military route is a killing knife.

769
34:20.719 --> 34:22.320
Now it's on our necks.

770
34:22.800 --> 34:24.110
Now we have to move it away

771
34:24.110 --> 34:25.570
and throw it on the ground.

772
34:25.880 --> 34:27.530
Otherwise, if we don't die today,

773
34:27.530 --> 34:28.730
we will die tomorrow.

774
34:28.760 --> 34:30.489
If not tomorrow, the day after.

775
34:30.889 --> 34:33.850
Are we just waiting to die?

776
34:35.550 --> 34:36.750
If our heads are gone,

777
34:36.820 --> 34:37.889
how can we advance?

778
34:38.469 --> 34:40.270
How can the revolution develop?

779
34:40.560 --> 34:43.520
Marxism emphasizes practice.

780
34:44.190 --> 34:47.190
In China, over 1,800 years ago,

781
34:47.670 --> 34:48.929
there were four words:

782
34:50.469 --> 34:52.199
seek truth from facts.

783
34:52.469 --> 34:55.590
Good, good, good.

784
35:28.110 --> 35:29.800
I'll have the same.

785
35:29.820 --> 35:31.050
Add more chili.

786
35:38.480 --> 35:39.730
Eat. Don't be shy.

787
35:43.130 --> 35:44.730
It's exchanged, here you go.

788
35:47.150 --> 35:53.590
[Nanchang Headquarters, Jiangxi]

789
35:59.620 --> 36:00.370
Darling,

790
36:01.590 --> 36:04.690
to commemorate the first anniversary of the New Life Movement,

791
36:04.690 --> 36:07.370
I wrote A Message to Our Compatriots.

792
36:08.810 --> 36:10.040
I'll read it to you.

793
36:12.410 --> 36:13.930
The New Life Movement

794
36:14.080 --> 36:17.030
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs of the Commission of Kuomintang]

795
36:14.170 --> 36:17.400
is truly the cornerstone of the new life of the Republic of China.

796
36:17.150 --> 36:20.530
[Soong Mei-ling, Wife of Chiang Kai-shek]

797
36:17.790 --> 36:19.570
Its purpose lies in our nation...

798
36:19.570 --> 36:20.410
Cornerstone?

799
36:20.610 --> 36:21.150
Yes.

800
36:21.350 --> 36:22.230
The stone

801
36:22.330 --> 36:23.300
at the corner...

802
36:24.440 --> 36:25.730
The will of people is

803
36:25.760 --> 36:30.630
the basis of any lasting republic.

804
36:30.670 --> 36:31.670
What does it mean?

805
36:32.830 --> 36:33.680
A basis.

806
36:34.750 --> 36:37.260
I feel that

807
36:38.640 --> 36:42.160
it's better to change cornerstone to basis.

808
36:42.220 --> 36:45.010
Wouldn't it be easier for the public to accept?

809
36:46.420 --> 36:47.620
Basis?

810
36:50.030 --> 36:51.470
When you were abroad,

811
36:51.680 --> 36:54.470
did Westerners use this word often

812
36:54.580 --> 36:56.310
when expressing this concept?

813
36:56.850 --> 36:58.480
What I just said

814
36:58.810 --> 37:00.470
is a quote from Machiavelli's

815
37:00.810 --> 37:03.690
Discourses on Livy.

816
37:04.070 --> 37:07.280
The New Life Movement is the foundation

817
37:07.930 --> 37:09.260
and the starting point.

818
37:10.510 --> 37:13.240
So what do you think of the word?

819
37:13.580 --> 37:14.410
How does it go?

820
37:14.850 --> 37:15.480
Basis.

821
37:15.670 --> 37:16.550
Basis.

822
37:17.130 --> 37:19.390
Alright, let's change it as you suggest.

823
37:19.630 --> 37:20.690
I'll change it now.

824
37:20.890 --> 37:23.350
Darling, you are my teacher of a single word.

825
37:26.260 --> 37:27.700
Basis.

826
37:27.770 --> 37:28.480
I learned another word.

827
37:28.480 --> 37:29.440
Basis.

828
37:29.460 --> 37:30.420
Basis.

829
37:34.400 --> 37:35.330
Generalissimo,

830
37:35.670 --> 37:36.350
Madame.

831
37:36.560 --> 37:38.550
The Ministry of Personnel just submitted

832
37:38.550 --> 37:41.070
the draft regulations for appointing generals.

833
37:39.100 --> 37:40.960
[Yan Daogang [Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

834
37:41.520 --> 37:43.580
Proposing 1 Special-Class General,

835
37:43.690 --> 37:45.090
8 First-Class Generals,

836
37:45.090 --> 37:46.400
and 20 Second-Class Generals.

837
37:46.400 --> 37:48.810
Here are the collar badge designs for the Special-Class General.

838
37:48.810 --> 37:50.810
We hope you can select one in person.

839
38:01.650 --> 38:02.730
Zurong,

840
38:03.260 --> 38:05.120
use the third one in the first row.

841
38:05.870 --> 38:06.760
Yes, sir.

842
38:07.540 --> 38:08.670
I plan to have them

843
38:08.940 --> 38:11.070
translate this article into English.

844
38:11.230 --> 38:13.360
Darling, please take a look at it then.

845
38:13.380 --> 38:14.230
Okay?

846
38:15.050 --> 38:16.900
We must let foreigners see

847
38:17.220 --> 38:18.340
that we Chinese

848
38:19.040 --> 38:20.840
will have a completely new look.

849
38:22.900 --> 38:29.430
[Shanghai]

850
38:23.800 --> 38:24.720
Sir,

851
38:25.590 --> 38:26.320
I copied a poem

852
38:26.320 --> 38:28.070
you wrote in May last year.

853
38:31.110 --> 38:35.070
A myriad families blackened faces buried in the weeds;

854
38:35.250 --> 38:38.480
Dare anyone sing a dirge that moves the earth?

855
38:38.850 --> 38:41.680
My vast thoughts connect to the boundless universe;

856
38:41.680 --> 38:45.500
[Xiao Jun, Left-wing Writer]

857
38:41.850 --> 38:45.650
Hear the startling thunder in the soundless place.

858
38:45.800 --> 38:48.280
[Lu Xun]

859
38:46.570 --> 38:48.610
Sir, when and where

860
38:48.720 --> 38:51.340
will this startling thunder occur?

861
38:51.880 --> 38:55.650
In a letter to a friend yesterday,

862
38:56.230 --> 38:59.760
I said something others might not believe.

863
39:00.590 --> 39:01.880
In China's affairs,

864
39:02.020 --> 39:03.350
when we take a step back,

865
39:03.540 --> 39:06.140
it's rare that the other side doesn't advance.

866
39:06.150 --> 39:08.150
Usually, they advance two steps.

867
39:08.400 --> 39:10.400
Unless we slap them hard in the face,

868
39:10.500 --> 39:13.580
they will never stop.

869
39:14.760 --> 39:16.320
Sir, you mean

870
39:16.380 --> 39:17.590
this startling thunder

871
39:17.590 --> 39:20.400
lies among those who resist the old forces

872
39:20.420 --> 39:22.460
most directly and resolutely?

873
39:27.000 --> 39:29.880
If China wants a thorough revolution,

874
39:31.500 --> 39:33.940
it needs us pen pushers,

875
39:35.330 --> 39:39.650
but it needs the gun barrels even more.

876
39:44.860 --> 39:46.380
This startling thunder,

877
39:46.930 --> 39:49.570
though seeming to rise from silence,

878
39:49.780 --> 39:52.710
is actually the accumulation of power in stillness.

879
39:53.140 --> 39:54.930
The moment it erupts,

880
39:55.270 --> 39:58.580
it will surely shatter the earth

881
39:59.020 --> 40:00.460
and create a new world.

882
40:18.870 --> 40:19.830
Slow down.

883
40:21.540 --> 40:22.620
Careful.

884
40:25.680 --> 40:26.600
Comrade Luofu,

885
40:35.500 --> 40:37.450
a lamp wick won't brighten unless trimmed,

886
40:37.450 --> 40:39.480
and truth won't become clear unless debated.

887
40:39.480 --> 40:41.280
The purpose of our meeting today

888
40:41.840 --> 40:44.280
is to explain the truth

889
40:44.710 --> 40:46.040
and clarify the issues.

890
40:46.190 --> 40:48.480
We cannot allow darkness under the lamp.

891
40:48.840 --> 40:50.790
If there is a patch of darkness here,

892
40:50.790 --> 40:53.790
a whole stretch of the revolution's path will be dark.

893
40:54.810 --> 40:55.730
Comrade Bo Gu,

894
40:56.000 --> 40:57.330
in your earlier speech,

895
40:57.520 --> 40:59.320
you mentioned a few objective reasons.

896
40:59.320 --> 41:01.360
But is that really the case?

897
41:02.190 --> 41:03.960
You said

898
41:04.020 --> 41:05.480
the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign failed

899
41:05.480 --> 41:06.360
because imperialism

900
41:06.360 --> 41:07.510
and the Kuomintang reactionaries

901
41:07.510 --> 41:08.590
were too powerful.

902
41:09.070 --> 41:10.280
But in our previous

903
41:10.280 --> 41:11.590
Counter-Encirclement Campaigns,

904
41:11.590 --> 41:13.050
the disparity in strength

905
41:13.510 --> 41:15.480
was always this stark.

906
41:16.480 --> 41:17.880
In the 1st Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

907
41:17.880 --> 41:20.110
the enemy had 100,000 men, and the Red Army 40,000.

908
41:20.110 --> 41:22.370
They outnumbered us two and a half to one.

909
41:22.630 --> 41:23.920
In the 2nd Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

910
41:23.920 --> 41:26.370
the enemy had 200,000 men, and we had about 34,000.

911
41:26.370 --> 41:28.440
The ratio was six to one.

912
41:28.920 --> 41:30.280
In the 3rd Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

913
41:30.280 --> 41:32.670
the enemy had 300,000 men, and we had 30,000.

914
41:32.670 --> 41:34.630
The ratio was ten to one.

915
41:35.070 --> 41:36.480
In the 4th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

916
41:36.480 --> 41:39.280
the enemy had 400,000 men, and we had about 70,000.

917
41:39.280 --> 41:41.190
The ratio was nearly six to one.

918
41:41.320 --> 41:43.150
In the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

919
41:43.150 --> 41:44.610
the enemy had 500,000 men,

920
41:44.710 --> 41:46.510
and we had over 100,000.

921
41:46.760 --> 41:49.190
The ratio was still five to one.

922
41:49.510 --> 41:51.550
Then why did we win the first four times,

923
41:51.550 --> 41:52.610
but lose this time?

924
41:52.920 --> 41:54.120
And lose so miserably

925
41:54.480 --> 41:56.560
that we couldn't even keep our territory

926
41:56.560 --> 41:58.290
and had to move out completely?

927
41:58.710 --> 41:59.440
You also said

928
42:00.390 --> 42:02.410
the base areas around the Central Soviet Area

929
42:02.410 --> 42:04.140
were fighting independently.

930
42:04.190 --> 42:05.480
But in the previous

931
42:05.700 --> 42:07.070
encirclement campaigns,

932
42:07.070 --> 42:08.630
didn't the enemy also divide

933
42:08.630 --> 42:09.630
our base areas?

934
42:09.800 --> 42:11.440
Back then, the base areas were smaller

935
42:11.440 --> 42:12.510
and weaker.

936
42:13.070 --> 42:15.920
You also said we did a poor job in the areas under Nationalist control.

937
42:15.920 --> 42:16.900
But such problems

938
42:16.900 --> 42:17.780
also existed

939
42:17.810 --> 42:19.610
during the previous campaigns.

940
42:19.840 --> 42:20.960
In comparison,

941
42:21.190 --> 42:23.280
before the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

942
42:23.280 --> 42:26.880
the people in the Central Soviet Area provided the best support.

943
42:27.030 --> 42:28.880
The Red Army's finances, food,

944
42:29.190 --> 42:30.000
and supplies

945
42:30.110 --> 42:31.880
were the most abundant.

946
42:32.080 --> 42:34.290
Then why did we still fail in the end?

947
42:35.360 --> 42:37.970
It shows that there were objective difficulties,

948
42:37.970 --> 42:40.100
but the main reasons were subjective.

949
42:43.400 --> 42:44.330
Today,

950
42:45.760 --> 42:47.280
I will summarize

951
42:48.070 --> 42:49.060
your mistakes.

952
42:50.000 --> 42:53.030
I think your mistakes can be divided into three stages.

953
42:53.030 --> 42:54.030
The first stage:

954
42:54.400 --> 42:56.440
adventurism in the offensive.

955
42:57.000 --> 42:58.000
The second stage:

956
42:58.310 --> 43:00.350
conservatism in the defensive.

957
43:00.800 --> 43:01.880
The third stage:

958
43:02.190 --> 43:03.960
flightism in the retreat.
